pounds to build a more  saturating snack or meal pairing a  banana for example with some nut butter  or an apple with some cheese would boost  the satiety factor  and leave you with some more stable  long-lasting energy levels  not to mention these combos are just  naturally intuitive because  they just taste really great next is to  include  snack foods in the right portions for  you so snack foods are delicious  and can undoubtedly be part of a healthy  and balanced diet  even for those trying to lose weight  however  as i discussed in my snack video here i  like to think of snacks as  mini meals not necessarily as treats  there are room for treats or what i  prefer to call fun foods as well but  they are a completely different  discussion well everyone's snacking  needs will be different  and you may prefer to have many moderate  sized  meals throughout the day instead of  three big meals plus snacks  generally speaking most people will want  a snack that's between a quarter  and half of the size of their formal  meal so trigger warning i'm going to  talk some numbers but  let's say your dinner is 600 calories as  a very  theoretical example that may mean like  150 to 300 calories for a snack  again these are just examples not rules  so choose a pattern of eating that works  best for you  next is to eat real desserts instead of  low calorie ones to feel  satisfied yes i love this advice  when embarking on a weight loss or  health journey a lot of people will turn  to  low calorie or diet options of their  favorite foods  as they feel as though this is what  they're allowed to have  however depending on the food and the  brand often these low calorie options  tend to be  bland chalky and lacking in what i call  the satisfaction factor  never mind being filled with additives  and artificial sweeteners to compensate  for their  lower calorie content what often ends up  happening is that we go on what i call  the satisfaction hunt we want the cookie  dough ice cream 