e crossed that line and the  likelihood of us keeping it up for any  measurable amount of time is nil  also fyi engaging in yoyo dieting or  weight cycling  is a hell of a lot more dangerous and  more detrimental to her health  than just staying at a higher weight i  don't know about you guys but  i can speak for myself when i say that i  most definitely  could not go the rest of my life eating  diet products  cutting out carbs or drinking weird  detox teas  in order to maintain a certain lower  weight  if the weight you're trying to maintain  requires some really extreme measures  and deprivation  in order to be sustained it's a really  good sign that it is not the healthiest  happiest weight for you as for all the  problematic advice we've seen  on one of the videos i watched there was  a very telling statement  that i think sums up the reason i'm even  doing this video today  it said i saw this on tik tok and i  wanted to try it myself  the content that we put on the internet  is for  everyone else in the world to see  assuming you have a public account  while viewers include people who are  able to write these types of videos off  as harmful or  bs it also includes those who are more  vulnerable to internalizing the  recommendations  and interpreting them as valuable health  advice as someone who has fallen victim  to the traps of diet culture in the past  well before we even had instagram it's  really scary how readily available this  information  is now today while i see a lot of  problematic content basically everywhere  i look  i think tick tock is a particular hotbed  due to its largely young age demographic  of the 800 million tick tock users  worldwide  over 25 are between the ages of 13 and  17  and nearly three-quarters of the app's  user's base  are between the ages of 13 and 24.  unfortunately  this age demographic coincides with the  peak age for developing an eating  disorder  or disordered eating all of that being  said  i can't blame the tick tock users i've  critiqued here  as they themselves are victims of diet  culture misinformation  and when something is so deeply  ingrained in our culture  it's really hard to escape all i can  suggest is to be mindful of the content  you create  share and consume on the internet and if  you are a creator  please acknowledge that all types of  people in  varying stages of their health and  wellness journeys  are able to access and be affected by  what you put out there  and on that note while we definitely  looked at some more positive content  today  i will personally be deleting the app  again  until i hear that there's some better  management and increased regulation for  the types of  potentially triggering pieces of content  that i've seen on tick tock  or i guess until you guys tell me to  make another video about this crap  so if you liked this video please be  sure to give it the thumbs up  leave me a comment below about what you  want to see me review next  subscribe to the channel and i will see  you next time on abby's kitchen  bye  you
 

